---
/*
 * Two incompatible tracker transports behind one interface, with the announce
 * state machine above it unchanged. The interface carries the accent because it
 * is the whole payoff: adding UDP meant one new class satisfying an existing
 * contract, with nothing upstream touched.
 *
 * Shared canvas and styling: the .diagram rules in src/styles/global.css.
 */
---

<figure class="diagram">
  <div class="diagram-scroll">
    <svg
      viewBox="-8 -10 596 240"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="transports-title transports-desc"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
    >
      <title id="transports-title">Two tracker transports behind one interface</title>
      <desc id="transports-desc">
        The announce state machine, with states stopped, connecting, waiting and error, sits above a
        single tracker interface. Two handlers implement that interface: an HTTP handler building a
        percent-escaped query and decoding a bencoded reply, and a UDP handler implementing BEP 15 with
        a hand-packed 98-byte payload. The state machine never learns which one it is talking to.
      </desc>

      <g class="edge-label">
        <text x="0" y="0">the state machine never learns which one it has</text>
      </g>

      <!-- The thing that must not change when a transport is added. -->
      <g class="node">
        <rect x="0" y="20" width="538" height="34" rx="3" />
      </g>
      <g class="field">
        <text x="14" y="42">announce state machine</text>
      </g>
      <g class="edge-label">
        <text x="524" y="42" text-anchor="end">stopped · connecting · waiting · error</text>
      </g>

      <g class="collapse">
        <line x1="269" y1="54" x2="269" y2="62" />
        <polygon points="263,62 269,76 275,62" />
      </g>

      <!-- The single contract both transports satisfy. -->
      <g class="accent">
        <rect x="0" y="82" width="538" height="34" rx="3" />
        <text x="14" y="104">one tracker interface</text>
      </g>

      <!-- Two implementations, neither known to the state machine. -->
      <g class="edge">
        <line x1="132" y1="116" x2="132" y2="150" />
        <line x1="406" y1="116" x2="406" y2="150" />
      </g>

      <g class="node">
        <rect x="0" y="150" width="264" height="56" rx="3" />
        <rect x="274" y="150" width="264" height="56" rx="3" />
      </g>
      <g class="field">
        <text x="14" y="172">HTTP handler</text>
        <text x="288" y="172">UDP handler, BEP 15</text>
      </g>
      <g class="offset">
        <text x="14" y="194">percent-escaped, bencoded</text>
        <text x="288" y="194">98 bytes at fixed offsets</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <figcaption>
    Adding the UDP transport meant one class against an existing contract, and no change above the
    interface.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
